      "message": "test(browser-supervisor): concurrency race probes + post-research\n\nExtends the SQL canary with Phase G: three genuine multi-session races\nagainst the real PostgreSQL 17 server, asserted deterministically.\n\n- race A: 20 concurrent enqueues of one idempotency key -> exactly one\n  fresh insert, 19 replay readbacks, identical command id, one row\n  (ON CONFLICT speculative-insert wait under READ COMMITTED)\n- race B: 10 concurrent clients contend for one broadcast command ->\n  exactly one lease holder (FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED)\n- race C: 10 commands drained by 10 concurrent clients -> every command\n  leased exactly once, no double-lease\n\nRace A's command is isolated to a non-leasing client so the races stay\nindependent (caught by the first local run). Racer SQL parenthesizes\njsonb extractions: ->> and || share precedence and left-associate.\n3/3 stable local passes on real PG 17.11 before push.\n\nPost-research records the jsonb NULL operator lessons, the corrected\nlane topology (lease_v3 is now the budget-guarded lane; lease_v2 routes\nto lease_control_v4), and the remaining weaknesses.",
